{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1033215-using-sorcery-instead-of-thaumaturgy-for-tremere","id":1033215,"title":"Using sorcery instead of Thaumaturgy for Tremere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-17T01:01:45-08:00","id":1033215,"title":"Using sorcery instead of Thaumaturgy for Tremere","content":"Hi everyone, I posted this in the Vampire forum as well.<br /> <br /> I'm doing an all Tremere game (we just finished character creation and prelude) and I've decided it would be cool to use Sorcery from the WOD books Sorcerer and Sorcerer Revised.<br /> <br /> I like Sorcery because it's more like awakened magic than Thaumaturgy is (though far more limited), you roll an attribute plus an ability when you want to work Sorcerery, spend a point of willpower (in this case it will be blood instead, as with Thaumaturgy) and then you allocate your successes on the various aspects of the effect.<br /> <br /> With Thaumaturgy, you roll willpower (diff=3+path level in use) and if you get one success or more the effect succeeds, additionall successes might give a minor perk to the spella aside from this, the effect of a spell is the same every time and this feels a lot more like DnD magic than Mage to me.<br /> <br /> I think that Sorcery is more versatile and exciting, I have a lot of experience storytelling with it (to say nothing of the more complex and hard to manage awakened magic) and I think my players will enjoy it.<br /> <br /> Like I said, this is an all Tremere Chronicle so power balance can be managed by putting more powerful obstacles in the way of the characters and since everyone will have Sorcery in the coterie, I don't see power imbalance within the group as an issue. <br /> <br /> I've run Mage, I've dealt with starting characters reading someones mind in the past and future from their sanctum on the other side of the earth so using sorcery (which my group knows well) doesn't intimidate me.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any thoughts or suggestions for me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:59:01-08:00","id":1033332,"title":"","content":"Just remember that Thamaturgy is quicker than Sorcery so cambat magic will change in respect to thier enemies that use fast acting diciplines. But if they are expierenced Sorcerer players that shouldnt matter. Otherwise it sounds like fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T07:44:22-08:00","id":1033355,"title":"","content":"Balance wise it is to consider that not necessarily all PC's want as much as possible in magic.<br /> <br /> I would go all the way and make all the Disciplines as Paths of Sorcery (for Tremere).<br /> <br /> Bit more work up front, but it would emphasize the Bloodmagic theme even more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T09:13:09-08:00","id":1033395,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine that Sorcery should still require a point of WP, not blood. Blood points should only be expended on Thaumaturgy and other Vampire exclusive things.<br /> If you're doing Sorcery the mundane way, then the limitations of WP should be a big deal. It's one of the reasons why mundane sorcerers can't fire off spells as easily and as often as their awakened counterparts.<br /> <br /> That being said, I am really limited in my Vampire knowledge, so perhaps bloodmagic is more similar to Sorcery than I know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T00:36:13-08:00","id":1033909,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the helpful points","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T01:39:26-08:00","id":1033920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1033215-using-sorcery-instead-of-thaumaturgy-for-tremere?p=1033395#post1033395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd imagine that Sorcery should still require a point of WP, not blood. Blood points should only be expended on Thaumaturgy and other Vampire exclusive things.<br /> If you're doing Sorcery the mundane way, then the limitations of WP should be a big deal. It's one of the reasons why mundane sorcerers can't fire off spells as easily and as often as their awakened counterparts.<br /> <br /> That being said, I am really limited in my Vampire knowledge, so perhaps bloodmagic is more similar to Sorcery than I know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire blood sorcery is faster (at least in terms of Path powers) because they usually go off within the turn. Path powers also require blood points, whereas vampire Rituals rarely do. This being different from mortal Sorcery, which has WP costs for everything. It makes it so that vampires can be a lot more aggressive, both in casting magic and in refueling their blood stores. A magic game using Vampire's system is has subtle but profound differences to the mortal Sorcery game.<br /> <br /> Which kind of makes me wonder if it wouldn't be a good idea to try running Thaumaturges that use Sorcerer's system, wholly or in part. Making even Path powers require time and the use of Instruments, raising the difficulty of effects by +1 across the board, and/or making Rituals cost something (whether that's BP or WP) could be used to modify how powerful Thaumaturgy is. It would certainly go a ways towards limiting the oft complained about &quot;OP&quot; nature of blood sorcery. I personally wouldn't use all of these changes at once - any one of them could accomplish what I want, without going way overboard.<br /> <br /> Then again, I'm one of those folks who thinks mortal Sorcerer rules are really harsh, and would use one of the variants that make it easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T16:12:06-08:00","id":1034309,"title":"","content":"I think I'm beginning to like the idea of blood sorcery being slower and more involved than Thaumaturgy. It would at least allow for there to be a trade-off between versatility and immediately usable powers for tactical combat, whereas currently someone practicing Thaumaturgy has the advantage of both. (Plus, the tendency of published characters to have discipline+path dots way in excess of what most vampires of similar age have in straight up disciplines, which compounds the THAUMATURGY RULES! bias.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}